WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.700
<v Mike>TMNT 2, the arcade game.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.620
<v Mike>You may have Shredder double teamed, but he still has you outnumbered.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.580
<v Mike>TMNT 2, the arcade game.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:32.380
<v Mike>And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.380
<v Hosts>I'm Mike.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.880
<v Hosts>I'm Sean.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.160
<v Hosts>And I'm Joe.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.860
<v Mike>Is it possible to be outnumbered while you're being double teamed?

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:48.180
<v Joe>Yeah, I mean, that was a little bit of a weird, because being double teamed implies that there's two to one against you.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.780
<v Mike>Right, but I guess he has the whole entire Foot Clan.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.000
<v Sean>Right. What are we talking about?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.460
<v Mike>The back of the box?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.360
<v Mike>Double teamed? The turtle? Oh yeah, the feet.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.380
<v Mike>Oh. So here's what they call, they're called the Foot Clan because they have more toes than the Ninja Turtles.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.720
<v Mike>So they're bragging.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:07.860
<v Mike>They're like, look at us.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.180
<v Sean>We have real feet.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.340
<v Mike>True feet. We have feet.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.960
<v Sean>Yeah. I like that.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.980
<v Mike>Turtles have three fingers and three toes.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.080
<v Mike>Is that the end of the episode?

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.060
<v Mike>What happened? I was just going to say that all about do it.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.260
<v Mike>No comment? Yeah.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.720
<v Sean>Geez. No comment.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:24.960
<v Mike>Rough crowd. It's fine.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.280
<v Joe>We're all stunned by that fact of turtles.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:33.100
<v Mike>They're saying double teamed on the back of the box because you can play this two player at the same time.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.860
<v Mike>And, you know, take that is the preferred way to play any beat them up.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:48.480
<v Mike>It's like if there were two player beat them up, if it was four player beat them up, if it's six player beat them up, it's always best to play with the maximum number of players on screen because that's the most chaos.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.880
<v Mike>That's the most button mashing satisfaction.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.920
<v Mike>That's the most like way to stay alive in the game because you don't have to deal with all six at the same time.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.240
<v Mike>You can have your friends help you out.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:09.100
<v Mike>And that was clearly the intention with the game that this is based on, which is, of course, the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles arcade game here on the NES.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:17.400
<v Mike>It is not a sequel to the first NES game, which we, you know, I don't want to say we were like harsh on it or whatever.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.940
<v Mike>We just weren't fans of it.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.200
<v Mike>It certainly gets a worse rap maybe than we gave it.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:30.360
<v Mike>So I think like in general, TMNT is a franchise we like and we want to like these games.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:41.360
<v Mike>And this one took the arcade game and brought it right to the NES with more levels and more boss fights and new features.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:50.140
<v Mike>So like who's to say that the old adage of the arcade game always being better than the 8-bit counterpart is true here.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.640
<v Mike>We're going to give this a real shake.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.160
<v Sean>I didn't know that there were more levels.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.400
<v Sean>I've never been very good at this game in the arcade.

