00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:29.220
<v Mike>If you've ever looked at the arcade game or played it, it feels like it's, you know, a direct adaptation of the very, very popular cartoon.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:41.480
<v Mike>It's it's using that same art style and it's the cut scenes and the pixel art are doing that much better than the NES could hope to.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:52.240
<v Mike>So I think for me, this is the one that like I like grab my eyes a lot at the arcade was like, whoa, this is basically the cartoon now as a video game.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:05:11.240
<v Mike>And regardless of how you feel about beat them ups, it's the same reason why like the Simpsons arcade game and the X-Men arcade game are like fondly remembered, not just because they're good beat them ups, but because it's like it's taking the art style of that thing that you like.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:23.240
<v Mike>And the world of that thing that you like and making it into a fun little mindless video game where like the the characters that you've come to expect all make appearances.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:30.540
<v Mike>And you're just kind of like, OK, I died time to put in another quarter to keep experiencing what's happening.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.000
